CricApp — Premium UI/UX Spec (Admin + Public)

Goal: Deliver a premium mobile-first experience for CricApp that feels modern, performant, and trustworthy. Two distinct interfaces: Public (fans, players) and Admin (match managers, scorers). Shared design system, consistent patterns, and prioritized performance.

Executive summary

Platform: Mobile-first responsive. Native feel via PWA; option to wrap in WebView later.

Look & feel: Modern, elevated (soft shadows, glass surfaces, 2xl rounded corners), micro-interactions, 60fps transitions.

Tone: Fast, confident, data-first. Emphasize live updates, clarity of scores, and admin efficiency.

Delivery: Preview UI → tasks → implement (Enhance-V7 flow). Default APPLY=NO.

Product personas & primary journeys

Public (Fan)

Quick discovery of live matches, leaderboard, match details, notifications.

Lightweight bottom nav: Home, Matches, Scorecard (live), Leaderboard, Profile.

Micro-interactions: animated score tick, pull-to-refresh, skeleton loaders.

Admin (Manager / Scorer)

Quick match creation, player/team management, in-match scoring console, match lifecycle (start/finish), audit logs.

Persistent bottom toolbar with high-priority actions: Start Match, Quick Score, Pause, End.

Real-time control panel with optimistic UI, undo, and replay of last actions.

Core features (MVP + Premium)
Public view (MVP)

Home feed: upcoming matches, pinned highlights.

Matches list: filter by series, date, team.

Live match view: ball-by-ball feed, scoreboard, player stats.

Leaderboard: sortable by runs, wickets, averages. Live sync.

Notifications: match start, innings end, milestones.

Profile: saved teams, preferences.

Admin view (MVP)

Dashboard: active matches, pending approvals, quick stats.

Match CRUD: create, schedule, toss, assign umpires, set overs.

Scoring console: ball entry, extras, change striker, wicket flow, undo.

Players & Teams: add/edit/import CSV.

Match lifecycle: Start → Pause → Resume → Complete (with validations).

Audit & export: CSV / PDF match scorecards.

Premium / Nice-to-have

Dark mode + theme switcher.

Realtime presence indicators (who’s scoring).

Rich charts: win probability, worm chart.

Live commentary microinteractions (emoji reactions).

Admin bulk actions & role management.

UI Patterns & Components (Design System)

Base tokens (Tailwind config): primary #1E3A8A, accent #06B6D4, bg #0F172A, surface white/soft, radius 2xl.

Typography: system font stack + bold headline, 16px base, responsive scales.

Components:

BottomNav (5 tabs public) — sticky, elevated card, haptic feedback.

AdminBottomBar — floating action cluster with primary CTA (Start/Quick Score).

ScoreCard — compact & expanded view. Shows overs, run rate, wickets.

BallTicker — animated microcomponent for each ball entry.

MatchForm — stepper: teams → overs → toss → schedule.

Modal/Drawer patterns for quick edits.

Toast & snackbar for confirmations with undo.

Interaction/UX rules

Always show skeleton loaders for network latency >200ms.

Use optimistic updates for admin scoring with server reconciliation; show small spinner if reconciliation pending.

Undo window 7s with action queue.

When an event is deleted, leaderboard recalculation happens instantly in-memory and via background reconciliation. UI shows “Recalculating…” banner if needed.

Accessibility: WCAG AA colors, keyboard focusable, aria labels for live scores (aria-live="polite").

